# build artifacts (reproducible via cargo build)
target/
# generated vectors (reproducible via tools/gen.py, seed 42)
vectors/
# raw node outputs (reproducible via tools/parity.py); keep *.json evidence
results/sums.f64
results/counts.i64

# --- ts/ (@numfast/kernels) -------------------------------------------------
# node_modules and dist are BUILD OUTPUTS of `cd numfast-native/ts && npm run
# build`, which also writes dist/BUILD.json recording the sha256, export count
# and i64 list of the .wasm it copied. Nothing under dist/ belongs in git:
# `ts/dist/bridge.js` was hand-committed with no tsconfig, no source map and no
# provenance, which is exactly how a build output becomes a stale artefact that
# nobody can trace. The fixtures under ts/test/fixtures ARE committed -- they
# are the recorded output of the Python host, not a build product.
ts/node_modules/
ts/dist/

# The 10 MB of tracked .bin fixtures that used to live in ts/artifacts/ are
# gone from version control because nothing needs them: qlookup.ts regenerates
# them (`node ts/qlookup.ts --gen [n]`) and demo.html now generates its own
# input in the browser from the same seed-42 LCG. A committed binary fixture
# that a script can reproduce is 10 MB of git history for nothing.
ts/artifacts/*.bin
